# check_wiring on COM11 @ 115200

[loopback]   success=True  raw=-
             no echo (expected for Roomba — Tx is connected only to the robot, not back to our Rx).
[awake-try]  success=False  raw=-
             no reply within 1 s.
[wake+DTR]   success=False  raw=-  banner=0 B
             no reply (banner=0 B, mode=)

[fallback]   retrying at 19200 baud ...
             success=False raw=-  detail=no reply within 1 s.

FAIL: no reply from Roomba.
Most likely causes, in order:
  1. Rx and Tx are swapped. The cable's TX should go to Roomba pin 3 (RxD into Roomba); the cable's RX should go to Roomba pin 4 (TxD from Roomba). Swap them.
  2. No ground. The cable's GND must be tied to Roomba pin 6 or 7.
  3. BRC not on a controllable line. We tried pulsing DTR, but your cable may wire BRC to RTS, or to nothing. Try pulsing manually (tie BRC to GND briefly) and rerun.
  4. TTL voltage mismatch. The Roomba expects 3.3-5 V TTL. If your adapter is true RS-232 (±12 V) without a level shifter, you may have damaged the input.
  5. Baud rate. Default is 115200; we also tried 19200 as a fallback.
